tage. The Democratic nominee withdrew from the race in late July, leaving independent Todd Achilles as the main challenger, which has generated some media interest but no clear evidence of a competitive race.\n\nThe polling record is thin and inconsistent, ranging from a lopsided Risch lead to a single outlier showing the challenger ahead, while prediction markets uniformly price Risch above 90 percent. Every major race rating service places this in the Safe or Solid Republican column. The expected outcome is a Risch victory by roughly fourteen points, with modest uncertainty given the unusual candidate configuration.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}]}